examples.question_text:
The graph has the form $y=\dfrac{k}{x}$ and passes through $(3,-2)$. Find $k$ and hence its equation.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\begin{axis}[width=75mm,height=75mm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,->},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},xmin=-5,xmax=5,ymin=-5,ymax=5,xtick={-4,-2,2,4},ytick={-4,-2,2,4},samples=100]
\addplot[curveBlue,thick,<->,domain=-4.7:-1.3] {-6/x};
\addplot[curveBlue,thick,<->,domain=1.3:4.7] {-6/x};
\addplot[curveBlue,only marks,mark=*] coordinates {(3,-2)};
\node[anchor=north east,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:3,-2) {$(3,-2)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
For the $y$-intercept, let $x=0$.

$\begin{aligned}y&=\dfrac{2}{0+2}-1\\&=0\end{aligned}$

For the $x$-intercept, let $y=0$.

$\begin{aligned}0&=\dfrac{2}{x+2}-1\\1&=\dfrac{2}{x+2}\\x+2&=2\\x&=0\end{aligned}$

Both intercepts are $(0,0)$. The asymptotes are $x=-2$ and $y=-1$.

From $y=\dfrac{1}{x}$, stretch vertically by factor $2$, then translate left $2$ units and down $1$ unit. Since $k>0$, the branches lie above-right and below-left of the intersection of the asymptotes.

A point on the left branch is found by letting $x=-3$: $y=\dfrac{2}{-3+2}-1=-3$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{asymRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\begin{axis}[width=80mm,height=80mm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,->},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},xmin=-6,xmax=5,ymin=-6,ymax=5,xtick={-4,-2,2,4},ytick={-4,-2,2,4},samples=100]
\addplot[asymRed,dashed] coordinates {(-2,-6) (-2,5)};
\addplot[asymRed,dashed] coordinates {(-6,-1) (5,-1)};
\addplot[curveBlue,thick,<->,domain=-5.7:-2.42] {2/(x+2)-1};
\addplot[curveBlue,thick,<->,domain=-1.65:4.7] {2/(x+2)-1};
\addplot[curveBlue,only marks,mark=*] coordinates {(0,0) (-3,-3)};
\node[anchor=south west,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:0,0) {$(0,0)$};
\node[anchor=north east,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:-3,-3) {$(-3,-3)$};
\node[anchor=north east,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:-2,4.7) {$x=-2$};
\node[anchor=north east,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] at (axis cs:4.8,-1) {$y=-1$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

